WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.659 --> 00:00:17.760
Vinnie and Mandy moved closer to the ship being tied to the dock.

2
00:00:19.001 --> 00:00:23.282
The Redcoat captain was speaking to a tall man in a black hat.

3
00:00:24.562 --> 00:00:31.244
He wore a long coat, pants that ended just below his knees, white stockings, and black shoes.

4
00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:40.946
"Mr. John Hancock," the captain read from a paper, "by order of His Royal Highness, King George III

5
00:00:40.966 --> 00:00:43.307
of England, you are under arrest."

6
00:00:44.868 --> 00:00:45.749
"What have I done?"

7
00:00:46.249 --> 00:00:48.211
John Hancock asked calmly.

8
00:00:48.231 --> 00:00:56.316
"Your ship, The Liberty, is carrying illegal tea into Boston Harbor," said the captain.

9
00:00:57.677 --> 00:01:01.960
Before John Hancock could say anything, the soldiers took him away.

10
00:01:03.272 --> 00:01:05.473
The men on the dock followed angrily.

11
00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:10.175
One of them saw Vinnie and Mandy and quickly walked over.

12
00:01:10.195 --> 00:01:12.896
"What are your names?"

13
00:01:13.556 --> 00:01:15.377
he asked when he got close.

14
00:01:16.638 --> 00:01:21.120
"I'm Vinnie, and this is my sister Mandy," said Vinnie bravely.

15
00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:23.761
"Are you American patriots?"

16
00:01:24.421 --> 00:01:25.221
the man asked.

17
00:01:25.241 --> 00:01:27.402
"Yes, sir!"

18
00:01:27.902 --> 00:01:29.003
Vinnie said proudly.

19
00:01:29.023 --> 00:01:31.644
"Good," the man said.

20
00:01:32.788 --> 00:01:35.991
He took out a piece of paper and wrote something on it.

21
00:01:36.011 --> 00:01:39.814
"You must find John Adams and give this to him.

22
00:01:40.915 --> 00:01:41.495
Go quickly.

23
00:01:42.716 --> 00:01:43.897
No one will suspect you."

24
00:01:45.318 --> 00:01:46.199
"Yes, sir."

25
00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:49.222
Vinnie saluted, but the man didn't see.

26
00:01:50.282 --> 00:01:53.065
He had already moved away to rejoin the others.

27
00:01:53.085 --> 00:01:56.648
"Vinnie! Why did you say that?"

28
00:01:57.348 --> 00:01:58.049
Mandy said.

29
00:01:58.069 --> 00:02:01.672
"We don't even know who those men are!"

30
00:02:03.004 --> 00:02:04.045
"John Hancock?

31
00:02:04.325 --> 00:02:05.166
John Adams?

32
00:02:05.686 --> 00:02:06.807
Come on, Mandy.

33
00:02:07.248 --> 00:02:08.349
We are in Boston.

34
00:02:09.710 --> 00:02:11.832
These are the founders of our country!"

35
00:02:12.332 --> 00:02:13.693
Vinnie said passionately.

36
00:02:13.713 --> 00:02:17.997
"Right now, America is under British rule.

37
00:02:18.457 --> 00:02:19.458
We must help."

38
00:02:19.478 --> 00:02:22.361
"So what can we do?"

39
00:02:23.001 --> 00:02:23.562
she asked.

40
00:02:23.582 --> 00:02:30.628
"Just as the man said, we must find John Adams," explained Vinnie.

41
00:02:31.804 --> 00:02:34.845
The children walked down the busy Boston streets.

42
00:02:36.246 --> 00:02:39.647
Horses, carriages, and wagons were everywhere.

43
00:02:40.868 --> 00:02:42.969
Women were in simple cotton dresses.

44
00:02:44.309 --> 00:02:46.010
Men wore three-cornered hats.

45
00:02:47.251 --> 00:02:52.633
As they approached an intersection, Vinnie and Mandy heard shouting and clapping.

46
00:02:52.653 --> 00:02:55.554
"What's going on?"

47
00:02:56.015 --> 00:02:56.855
Vinnie wondered.

48
00:02:58.115 --> 00:03:03.171
On the next street, a crowd was gathered in front of a man standing on a barrel.

49
00:03:04.453 --> 00:03:06.174
He looked excited and angry.

50
00:03:06.194 --> 00:03:09.657
"Should we pay taxes to the British?"

51
00:03:10.098 --> 00:03:10.798
he shouted.

52
00:03:10.818 --> 00:03:15.102
"No!" the crowd cheered.

53
00:03:15.122 --> 00:03:17.805
"We have no vote!

54
00:03:19.086 --> 00:03:21.408
We have no one to speak for us in England!"

55
00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:23.089
the man continued.

56
00:03:24.230 --> 00:03:25.692
People shouted loudly.

57
00:03:27.084 --> 00:03:29.366
"The Redcoats take over our homes!

58
00:03:30.507 --> 00:03:32.449
We pay too much for our tea!

59
00:03:33.830 --> 00:03:36.713
We even pay too much to mail our letters!"

60
00:03:37.273 --> 00:03:38.114
cried the man.

61
00:03:38.134 --> 00:03:40.336
"Who is he?"

62
00:03:41.056 --> 00:03:43.418
Mandy asked a boy standing nearby.

63
00:03:43.438 --> 00:03:45.620
"That's Mr.

64
00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:48.022
Keith, the grocer," said the boy.

65
00:03:48.042 --> 00:03:50.324
"Why is he shouting?"

66
00:03:50.885 --> 00:03:51.546
asked Vinnie.

67
00:03:52.747 --> 00:03:54.108
The boy stared at them.

68
00:03:55.412 --> 00:03:57.474
"You aren't from Boston, are you?"

69
00:03:57.954 --> 00:03:58.454
he said.

70
00:03:58.474 --> 00:04:01.697
"King George signed the Stamp Act.

71
00:04:02.777 --> 00:04:07.141
The law makes us pay extra money, a tax, for everything we buy.

72
00:04:08.381 --> 00:04:10.463
Everyone is very angry about it."

73
00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:16.647
"I never knew America was like this once," Mandy whispered to
